    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## HubSpot to NetSuite Sales Order and Invoice Sync\n\n**Closed Won deal → NetSuite sales order.** When a HubSpot deal moves to Closed Won, the workflow finds the NetSuite customer by the contact's email (or creates one), saves the NetSuite customer ID on the HubSpot contact, and creates the sales order, or updates it if one already exists for the deal.\n\n**NetSuite invoices → HubSpot.** Every 15 minutes, invoices changed in NetSuite update the deal's **Invoice Status**: Invoiced, Partially Paid, or Paid in Full.\n\n**Failures → Slack.** Any error posts the deal, the NetSuite error, and a link to the execution.\n\n### Setup\n**HubSpot:** create a private app with these scopes: `crm.objects.deals.read`, `crm.objects.deals.write`, `crm.objects.contacts.read`, `crm.objects.contacts.write`, `crm.objects.line_items.read`. Add a **HubSpot Service Key** credential with its access token. Create the properties `netsuite_customer_id` (contact, text), `invoice_status` (deal, dropdown: Invoiced, Partially Paid, Paid in Full), and optionally `netsuite_item_id` (product and line item, text). In the app's **Webhooks** tab, subscribe to deal property changes for `dealstage`, sent to this workflow's production webhook URL.\n\n**NetSuite:** enable **REST Web Services** and **OAuth 2.0**, add a Free-Form Text transaction body field `custbody_hubspot_deal_id` applied to sales orders and invoices, and create an integration record using Authorization Code Grant with the REST Web Services scope. In n8n, create an **OAuth2 API** credential:\n- Authorization URL: `https://ACCOUNT_ID.app.netsuite.com/app/login/oauth2/authorize.nl`\n- Access Token URL: `https://ACCOUNT_ID.suitetalk.api.netsuite.com/services/rest/auth/oauth2/v1/token`\n- Scope: `rest_webservices`, Authentication: Header\n\nNetSuite's authorization-code tokens expire after 7 days, so reconnect the credential if NetSuite calls start returning 401.\n\n**Settings:** fill in your account ID, time zone, Closed Won stage IDs, and item, subsidiary, and currency IDs.\n\n**Slack:** connect Slack and pick a channel in **Alert on Slack**, then set **Workflow settings → Error workflow** to this workflow.",
        "height": 1300,
        "width": 640,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "12b154a1-c781-4053-b08d-6fa5bd94e6ac",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1400,
        -300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Triggers and settings\n**HubSpot Deal Webhook** receives HubSpot's deal stage change events. **Every 15 Minutes** starts the invoice check.\n\n**Settings** holds your NetSuite account and ID mappings. **Which Sync?** sends each run to the right flow.",
        "height": 1000,
        "width": 640,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "784313de-4a5b-4b2f-bead-e281d485437a",
      "name": "Start",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -720,
        -300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. HubSpot deal moves to Closed Won\n**Read Deal Events** keeps the latest stage change per deal from HubSpot's batched events. Deals that reached a stage in `closedWonStages` continue.\n\n**Get Deal** reads the deal with its contact and line items. A deal without a contact stops with an error.",
        "height": 600,
        "width": 1100,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "91e5a0fe-78f0-42bc-a586-eaaa244290ac",
      "name": "Section 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        -300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. Match or create the NetSuite customer\n**Find NetSuite Customer** looks up the contact's email with SuiteQL. If there's no match, **Create NetSuite Customer** creates one: a company customer when the contact has a company, otherwise an individual.\n\nThe NetSuite customer ID is saved on the HubSpot contact as `netsuite_customer_id`.",
        "height": 600,
        "width": 1500,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "d6d9462c-3d9d-47da-ad3e-1477456850f9",
      "name": "Section 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1060,
        -300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. Create or update the sales order\nEach line item uses its `netsuite_item_id`, or `genericItemId` from Settings. A deal with no line items is billed as one line for the deal amount.\n\n**Find Existing Sales Order** checks `custbody_hubspot_deal_id`, so a deal never creates two sales orders. An existing order is updated and its lines replaced.\n\nNetSuite errors stop the run with the deal ID, NetSuite's error, and the deal link.",
        "height": 640,
        "width": 1420,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "24903dc6-7f8c-4377-a674-51f073d3d492",
      "name": "Section 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2580,
        -300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4. Sync invoice status back to HubSpot\nEvery 15 minutes, invoices changed in the last `invoiceLookbackMinutes` that carry a HubSpot deal ID update the deal's `invoice_status`: Paid in Full, Partially Paid, or Invoiced.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 960,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "b1c5951f-9d07-4265-9f70-0d1fe3046dcf",
      "name": "Section 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        340
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 5. Slack alert when anything fails\nSet this workflow as its own error workflow. Any failure posts the step, the error, and a link to the execution.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 700,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "9369c52d-b91e-451c-bbdc-5a78dbc4b6f8",
      "name": "Section 5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        700
      ]
    }
  ],
